L32: The BRJ+vitamin C group exhibited significantly higher peak power (419 ± 98 W vs. 403 ± 103 W, P < 0.001) and peak power per body weight (6.2 ± 0.8 W/kg vs. 5.9 ± 0.8 W/kg, P < 0.001) compared to the placebo group in the upper-body WAnT (Table 2). Although mean power was higher in the BRJ+vitamin C group (260 ± 72 W vs. 246 ± 75 W, P = 0.099), this difference did not reach statistical significance. No significant differences were observed for minimum power, minimum power per body weight, mean power per body weight, time to peak power, or fatigue index (all P ≥ 0.05). No significant intervention-by-time interactions or carryover effects were detected (P > 0.05).
