L34: In the lower-body WAnT, the BRJ+vitamin C group showed significantly higher mean power (390 ± 89 W vs. 376 ± 89 W, P = 0.002) and mean power per body weight (5.8 ± 0.9 W/kg vs. 5.3 ± 0.8 W/kg, P = 0.001) compared to placebo (Table 3). No significant differences were observed for peak power, peak power per body weight, minimum power, minimum power per body weight, time to peak power, or fatigue index (all P ≥ 0.05). No significant intervention-by-time interactions or carryover effects were detected (P > 0.05).
